<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani bourse suspends member on default.</title>
<headline>Pakistani bourse suspends member on default.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's main Karachi Stock Exchange (KSE) said on Tuesday it had suspended a member for default.</p>
<p>A KSE statement said the membership of M. Rashid Jamal was suspended for failing to pay money he owed in share transactions and to deliver sold shares on Tuesday's settlement day.</p>
<p>It did not mention the amount involved.</p>
<p>Jamal was not immediately available for comment.</p>
</text>
